        "object": "<p>Speaking at the opening of the Venice film festival, the actor-director addressed why the jury of which she is chair will only be shown two films made by female film-makers</p><p>Maggie Gyllenhaal said there is a “systemic problem” that explains why only two female directors are in the running for the Golden Lion at the Venice film festival this year.</p><p>“It’s harder for women to get films financed,” said the actor-director, who is heading up the jury of the world’s oldest cinema showcase this year.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/sep/02/maggie-gyllenhaal-says-film-industry-has-a-systemic-problem-with-sexism\">Continue reading...</a>"
